MRJ 2.2.5 + Swing 1.1.1 Build Prerequisites
=============================================

Target: classic Mac OS 9.2.2, MRJ (Mac OS Runtime for Java) 2.2.5, with the
standalone Swing 1.1.1 add-on (Swing wasn't bundled with Java until 1.2).

ecj.jar  — reuse java14/ecj.jar or java13/ecj.jar (same compiler). Supports
           -target 1.1 (class file version 45), which matches MRJ 2.2.5's
           JDK 1.1.7/1.1.8 base. Minimum -source is 1.3 (ECJ doesn't accept
           -source below 1.3), but that only affects which language grammar
           is parsed, not the class files produced — fine for this codebase.

swing.jar  — INCLUDED. Genuine Swing 1.1.1 FCS release (Sun, 1999), core
             classes + Metal look-and-feel. Class file version 45 confirmed
             (matches JDK 1.1 bytecode). README from Sun's original release
             confirms: "This release relies on bug fixes first released in
             JDK 1.1.7" — matches MRJ 2.2.5 exactly.

mac.jar    — INCLUDED. Mac-specific look-and-feel from the same Swing 1.1.1
             release. Optional (Metal in swing.jar works without it), but
             appropriate given the target platform.

JDKClasses.zip — INCLUDED (pulled from real Mac OS 9.2.2 hardware, System
                 Folder:Extensions:MRJ Libraries:). This is the actual
                 bootclasspath equivalent to java13/rt.jar or java14/rt.jar —
                 confirmed contains java/lang/Object.class and the rest of
                 java.*, at class file version 45 (JDK 1.1 bytecode). Use this
                 as -bootclasspath / -Dcompile.bootclasspath.

MRJClasses.zip — INCLUDED (same source). Apple's native AWT peer/bridge layer
                 (com/apple/mrj/internal/awt/*) that JDKClasses.zip's AWT
                 implementation calls into at runtime. Not a compile-time
                 bootclasspath by itself (no java.* packages in it) — needed
                 on the classpath alongside JDKClasses.zip for AWT to actually
                 work at runtime on real hardware.

QTJava.zip — INCLUDED (same source). QuickTime for Java bindings. Not needed
             for this port; came along with the pull from hardware.

All three zips and the two Swing jars are gitignored — same reasoning as
java13/rt.jar and java14/rt.jar (build-time only, not committed).
